{# Negative Prompting: Explicit exclusion constraints with self-verification #}
Objective: {{ objective|default("Provide a direct, factual, and concise answer while strictly avoiding prohibited elements.") }}

<positive_guidelines>
{% if positive_guidelines %}
{% for item in positive_guidelines %}
- {{ item }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
- Be direct and factual.
- Use concise language.
{% endif %}
</positive_guidelines>

<negative_constraints>
{% if negative_constraints %}
{% for item in negative_constraints %}
- DO NOT {{ item }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
- DO NOT use vague or speculative language.
- DO NOT include irrelevant information or filler words.
- DO NOT make assumptions beyond what is explicitly given.
{% endif %}
</negative_constraints>

{% if forbidden_topics %}
<forbidden_topics>
{{ forbidden_topics }}
</forbidden_topics>
{% endif %}

<query>
{{ user_input|default(query|default("")) }}
</query>

Instructions:
1. Draft your answer.
2. In the <constraint_check> block, explicitly verify that your draft violates NONE of the <negative_constraints>.
3. Output the final, clean answer in <final_answer>.

<constraint_check>
Verify each constraint and confirm none are violated
</constraint_check>

<final_answer>
Your verified final answer after constraint check
</final_answer>
